  "abilities": [],
  "behavior": "It retains much of an adult Toe Biter's behavior, using combos, powerful attacks, and area hits. In O.R.C. encounters it often joins the fight directly alongside other creatures, so you will rarely face it completely alone.",
  "interactionWithPlayer": "It is somewhat tougher than a regular Toe Biter and can still apply venom and chill through its attacks. Its ranged attack remains unblockable, allowing it to punish you even while you are trying to focus on other enemies in the wave.",
  "interactionWithCreatures": "It often appears in O.R.C. groups and waves alongside different controlled creatures. Its large health pool lets it remain active for a long time while other enemies continue pressuring the player.",
  "strategy": "Use Spicy damage and especially avoid Stabbing weapons. Do not try to block its unblockable attack, and watch venom and chill buildup while other enemies are nearby. If the event allows turrets, use them against it because O.R.C. variants take roughly triple turret damage. If several threats appear at once, clear weaker enemies first so you can focus on the Toe Biter afterward.",
